  "summary": "Several studies apply transformer or transformer-adjacent architectures to sepsis early warning on ICU vital signs data. Haddad et al. [D0104] use transformer models for predicting sepsis onset before clinical recognition on the IEEE-CIS dataset, reporting an F1 of 0.675. Novak et al. [D0102] benchmark transformer models for the same task on the AgriSat dataset, achieving an AUROC of 0.6. Okafor et al. [D0103] also deploy transformer models for predicting sepsis onset on the AgriSat dataset, reporting an accuracy of 0.873. Novak et al. [D0101] apply attention-only encoder architectures (a transformer variant) to early detection of septic deterioration in intensive care on the HateCheck dataset, reporting a MAPE of 0.935. For comparison, Haddad et al. [D0106] address the same sepsis prediction task but with message-passing networks rather than transformers, reporting an F1 of 0.791 on the SentinelYield-2 dataset.",
